      "created_at": "2017-10-10T11:31:27Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-10-10T11:34:06Z",
      "body": "I've never received a confirmation by clicking agreeing to Terms and Conditions when checking out for a website?\r\n\r\nApparently, it's good enough that with the following (paraphrasing here):\r\n\r\n* The TOS is easily accessible at any time and the user can print it at any time.\r\n* If the user is forced to scroll down to the end of the TOS page before checking out, that's really good too.\r\n\r\nAlso if we store this data to the order upon checkout it should be sufficient though? I mean you're entering details at every checkout.\r\n\r\nMaybe we can include a link in confirmation email if TOS enabled too saying \"Thank you for signing up for your membership level etc. Here is a link to Terms Of Service which you agreed upon by signing up\".",
