      "created_at": "2018-04-25T15:07:54Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-04-25T15:07:54Z",
      "body": "GDPR discussions have given us reason to revisit this. We need to at the very least track that the TOS was checked at checkout either in the order data or in user meta... with a timestamp and the page that was agreed to.\r\n\r\nIdeally:\r\n* we keep track of every such time that users check the box and submit.\r\n* prompt users to agree again if we don't have data for their checking or the TOS has changed\r\n* allow for other types of agreements besides the TOS",
